- Simple test strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lightweight policy evaluation skeleton
function evaluatePolicy(event, policyStore) {
  // policyStore: { tenant_id: { redact: [fields] } }
  const p = policyStore[event.tenant_id] || { redact: [] };
  const redacted = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(event.payload || {}));
  p.redact.forEach(f => { if (redacted.hasOwnProperty(f)) redacted[f] = "***"; });
  return { ...event, payload: redacted };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend to support dynamic policy updates without downtime?
- What metrics would you monitor to ensure privacy and latency goals?

